      "title": "Reject non-integer window indices",
      "body": "The pair/order schema compares only values. Python treats True == 1 and 1.0 == 1 as true, so malformed TOML records pass the exact-order gate. A fresh independent synthetic 52-case process-2 record was accepted after separately replacing the first window pair or order with True or 1.0 (four accepted malformed variants). Require type(value) is int for both fields before equality, and preserve regression evidence for Boolean and floating-point variants."
    },
