      "start": 73,
      "end": 79,
      "title": "Validate stage exit and resource scalar schemas",
      "body": "The stage gate similarly accepts false as a successful returncode (False == 0), and the memory predicate accepts infinite available_kib or negative swap_used_kib because it only applies one-sided bounds. These are malformed/impossible process evidence, which the stated fail-closed audit must reject. Require integer exit codes and finite nonnegative integer KiB values (including terminal_memory); apply equivalent strict checks to stage numeric identity/limit fields used as admission evidence, and add synthetic stage-level malformed/missing tests. Existing offline tests cover raw records and pressure boundaries, but never exercise stage() evidence schema."
    }
